						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Two things . . .<br /><br />One, Sony doestnt care about EQ I anymore and havent since they saw the peaked interest with a new game launch in SWG.&nbsp; For proof, see the last 4 or 5 expansions with the exception of maybe PoP.&nbsp; The core design team was either really bored after year 1-3 of EQ&#039;s launch or left for other projects, inhouse or elsewhere.<br /><br />Two, EQ 2 as a whole (graphics, sound, playability, character balance, trade skilling, vastness, expansion capability, support, funding, concept, storyline, etc) blows EQ 1 away IMO.&nbsp; Its like saying you want to break our your Atari and play some football while someone else is playing X-Box or PS2&#039;s Maddens 2005.<br /><br />Its almost over.&nbsp; They have no plans to cancel EQ until every last paying member cancels their account, they are probably still breaking even on EQ 1 every month or making slight profits.&nbsp; I think they are only keeping EQ 1 for PR and Spin as to not completely alienate all EQ 1 players.&nbsp; They want that money too, in time, they will get it.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/banghead2.gif" alt="banghead2" border="0" /></td>
