							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: October 24, 2004, 07:35:43 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Ive been in since early August and its made a lot of strides since then, but, like others have posted, its not ready to launch next month.&nbsp; I hope they continue patches and large beta through Jan and then maybe launch in 1st Qtr 2005.<br /><br />People would be very impressed at that point with its launch.<br /><br />As a game, its very beautiful and very adventurous.&nbsp; Fast paced and well rounded.&nbsp; Things are very easy, very equalled, very compatible.&nbsp; I think a group of a Druid, Rogue, and Enchanter would do as well in a group encounter as a Cleric, Warrior, Shaman, if that helps explain the level of parody between classes in this game.<br /><br />I wish good and evil could join together, but understand they are trying to bring back the RP aspect of the game some more, EQ had lost that completely after year 1 IMO.<br /><br />Its also heavily shifted away from camps and grinds, and more to grouping, soloing, instanced zoning, questing, and missions.<br /><br />The world is immense and the graphics / sound are very rich.&nbsp; <br /><br /></td>
